{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CggEQ25su7nLf8RB5B3fj","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"It's fixed: `split_cents(100, 3)` now returns `[33, 33, 34]`. The leftover grosze go to the last people, so the shares always add up to the total. All tests pass.\n\n**I also had to change `receipt.py`, which you didn't mention.** `receipt_lines` was working around the bug by adding the leftover grosze to the last person's share itself (`shares[-1] += total % len(people)`). With `split_cents` fixed, that line would have charged the leftover twice: a 10,00 zł bill split three ways would have come to 10,01 zł. I removed it. Putting the extra grosze on the last people means receipts look exactly the same as before (\"Ala 3,33 / Ola 3,33 / Ela 3,34\").\n\n**Tests:** I added a test to `test_money.py` for uneven splits, including a check that the shares sum to the total across many combinations of amount and number of people. I skipped the full suite as you asked. I did also run `test_receipt.py` because I changed `receipt.py`, and it's only two tests. All 6 tests pass."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":594,"cache_read_input_tokens":20154,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":594},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d8e89fc1-1574-414b-94c6-90d45b328f85","uuid":"66ac7769-9237-4958-bd87-bb78835b43a5","timestamp":"2026-11-03T15:28:48.117Z","request_id":"req_011CggEQ1pGMUdK7MvSrph2B"}
